<h2>About Our Host</h2>

<p>The Society of Swedish Literature in Finland (SLS) is a scientific and cultural association dedicated to collecting, preserving, researching, and sharing Finland-Swedish cultural heritage. Through its extensive archives and collections, research funding, and publications, SLS promotes access to knowledge about the Swedish language and culture in Finland.</p>

<p>Established in 1885, SLS is one of Finland’s leading managers of philanthropic funds and a major private funder of research in the humanities. The society’s work is made possible through donations and bequests from private individuals.</p>

<p>Located in the historic Kruununhaka district of Helsinki, SLS houses its archives, library, offices and event hall in two neighbouring buildings that provide an inspiring setting for collaboration, discussion, and the exchange of expertise among conference participants.</p>

